WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.847
After tokenization, every token maps to an integer in the model vocabulary.

00:00:05.847 --> 00:00:09.652
The model does not directly receive the visible text.

00:00:09.652 --> 00:00:12.387
It receives token I D's.

00:00:12.387 --> 00:00:20.907
The code uses the same q w e n three zero point six billion checkpoint used throughout the local-model examples.

00:00:20.907 --> 00:00:28.597
We tokenize a short RAG sentence and then inspect both the token pieces and their numerical I D's.

00:00:28.597 --> 00:00:31.812
Remember that an I D is an identifier.

00:00:31.812 --> 00:00:35.852
A larger token I D does not mean the token is more important.
